          "session_id": "full-mt-m-004",
          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How long before it starts working?",
          "answer": "My search did not find how quickly a blue reliever inhaler starts to work, so I can't give you a time from the guidance.\n\nTwo passages are relevant to timing:\n\n- The \"Asthma\" condition summary (educational summary) says that an attack that doesn't respond to reliever treatment, or that returns within a few hours, needs prompt medical assessment.\n- The \"Sticking with asthma treatment\" summary (general clinical reference) says that a relief inhaler gives an immediate sensation of relief. It also says that rising reliever use is a sign that asthma may not be well controlled.\n\nIf your blue inhaler isn't helping, or your symptoms come back within a few hours, contact your clinician or asthma nurse promptly. Your written asthma action plan should say what to do and when to seek help.\n\nIf your breathing suddenly gets much harder, you struggle to speak, your lips or fingers look blue, or you feel drowsy or confused, seek emergency help straight away. Don't wait to see whether the inhaler works.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
